    {
      "title": "Tokens and Context Windows: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Tokens and Context Windows: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Token Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==token== is a **sub-word chunk**: about 4 English characters or 0.75 words",
                "The model reads and predicts ==tokens==, never raw characters or words"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Window and Billing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Input tokens",
                    "sub": "prompt + context",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Output budget",
                    "sub": "max_tokens",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Context window",
                    "sub": "one shared limit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Window = input + output; ==max_tokens== is carved out of the same window",
                "Going over the window {red:truncates or errors}",
                "Billing, latency and limits are all counted in tokens"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Input",
                "Output"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Counts toward window",
                  "yes",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Price per token",
                  "lower",
                  "==usually higher=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Counting and Attention",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tokenizers differ per model: the same text gives different counts",
                "Count with the **provider's tokenizer**, never word count, for limits",
                "Details in the ==middle== of a long prompt are recalled worse than the start or end"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Long context is not free attention",
              "text": "A bigger window fits more, but does not read it all equally well. Put key facts at the **start or end**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sampling Controls: Temperature and Top-p",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sampling Controls: Temperature and Top-p",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Sampling Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Model",
                    "note": "scores every token",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Distribution",
                    "note": "probability per token",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sampling",
                    "note": "temperature, top-p",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "One token",
                    "note": "appended, repeat",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Temperature vs Top-p",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Temperature} rescales the distribution: changes how ==flat== it is",
                "{purple:Top-p} (nucleus) keeps the ==smallest set== of tokens whose cumulative probability reaches p",
                "With `top_p=0.9`, sample only inside that set",
                "Tune ==one==, leave the other at default"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Temperature",
                "Behaviour"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`0`",
                  "near-deterministic (greedy)"
                ],
                [
                  "~0.7 to 1",
                  "varied"
                ],
                [
                  "above 1",
                  "{red:erratic}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which Setting to Use",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Temperature"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Extraction, classification",
                  "`0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Code, RAG answers",
                  "`0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Brainstorming, creative writing",
                  "higher"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "client.messages.create(",
                "    model=...,",
                "    temperature=0,",
                "    max_tokens=500,",
                "    messages=[...])"
              ],
              "note": "deterministic-style call"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not a guarantee",
              "text": "Temperature `0` does ==not== guarantee identical outputs across runs or model versions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "System vs User Prompts",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "System vs User Prompts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who Carries What",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "System prompt",
                "User message"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Holds",
                  "{blue:role, rules, tone, format}",
                  "{green:per-turn task and data}"
                ],
                [
                  "Lifetime",
                  "**every turn**",
                  "this turn only"
                ],
                [
                  "Cacheable",
                  "==yes==, it is stable",
                  "rarely, it changes"
                ],
                [
                  "Untrusted data",
                  "{red:never}",
                  "{green:fenced here}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlight": 1,
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stable instructions go in ==system== so they apply to every turn and can be **cached**",
                "Untrusted input and retrieved docs go in the ==user turn==, fenced: `<context>...</context>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example: Support Bot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "system = \"You are a support bot. Answer only from the provided context.\"",
                "user = (",
                "    \"Question: How do I reset my password?\\n\"",
                "    \"<context>\\n[doc1] Reset via Settings > Security.\\n</context>\"",
                ")"
              ],
              "note": "rules in system; question plus fenced context in user"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not a security boundary",
              "text": "Priority between system and user is a ==convention==. A system prompt can be **leaked** or overridden by ==prompt injection==."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pasting ==secrets or API keys== into the system prompt",
                "Burying critical rules at the **end** of a long user message",
                "Putting retrieved text in system, unfenced"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Structured Output with JSON Schemas",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Structured Output with JSON Schemas",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Levels of Strength",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Structured output== = model returns **parseable JSON** that matches a schema",
                "Code consumes it directly, {green:no regex}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Level",
                "Guarantee"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Prompt asks for JSON",
                  "{red:Weakest}: any text may come back"
                ],
                [
                  "JSON mode",
                  "Valid JSON, **any shape**"
                ],
                [
                  "Schema or tool call",
                  "{green:Enforces the schema}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Schema",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`type`: object, string, number",
                "`properties`: the fields allowed",
                "`required`: fields that must appear",
                "`enum`: only these values",
                "`additionalProperties:false`: no extra fields"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{\"type\":\"object\",",
                "\"properties\":{",
                "\"sentiment\":{\"enum\":[\"pos\",\"neg\",\"neu\"]},",
                "\"score\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},",
                "\"required\":[\"sentiment\",\"score\"]}"
              ],
              "note": "sentiment is limited to three labels"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Validate and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Call model",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parse JSON",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "sub": "Pydantic / Zod",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Retry",
                    "sub": "on failure",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Forgetting `required`: fields silently missing",
                "Free text where an `enum` fits: unpredictable labels",
                "`max_tokens` cuts the JSON off mid-object"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Syntax is not correctness",
              "text": "Valid JSON can still hold ==wrong values==. Always validate in code and retry."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grounding and RAG Prompt Templates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Grounding and RAG Prompt Templates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Why Models Hallucinate",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The model predicts ==plausible text== from training patterns, not verified facts",
                "It has **no built-in** \"I don't know\"",
                "==Grounding== puts retrieved passages in the prompt: answer from evidence, not memory"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. RAG Flow",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Embed",
                    "sub": "the query",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Retrieve",
                    "sub": "top-k chunks",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Build prompt",
                    "sub": "with chunks",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Generate",
                    "sub": "the answer",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Template and Citations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "SYSTEM: Answer only from the context.",
                "Cite sources like [doc2].",
                "Otherwise say \"I don't know\".",
                "<context>",
                "[doc1] chunk text",
                "[doc2] chunk text",
                "</context>",
                "QUESTION: {question}"
              ],
              "note": "rules, then context, then question"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tag every chunk with a ==source ID==",
                "Require citations like `[doc2]` so answers can be checked"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Irrelevant or too many chunks: ==noise== and lost-in-the-middle",
                "No ==refusal instruction==",
                "No check that the answer is supported by the context"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Rules, then `<context>` with source IDs, then the question. Say: **answer only from context, else don't know**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
